# Personal config layer — PRIVATE. See docs/concepts/configuration-model.md.
# Everything under top-level config/ is YOUR data (identity, repo list, agent
# registry, custom skills) and must never enter this PUBLIC framework repo via
# `git add .`. Only config/README.md is tracked. In your own PRIVATE deployment
# fork you DO commit config/ — drop these two lines there, or `git add -f`.
# (The examples/ tree holds placeholders only and is safe to commit.)
/config/*
!/config/README.md
*.private-key.pem
*.pem
.env.local

